---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ToolCard from '../../components/ToolCard.astro';
import SurveyDashboard from '../../components/SurveyDashboard';
import {activeTools} from '../../data/tools';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import researchPhoto from '../../assets/pathways/investigate.jpg';
import fieldPhoto from '../../assets/pathways/explore.jpg';
---
<Base title="Investigate fungi">
<div class="station-page">
  <section class="station-hero station-hero-split">
    <div class="station-hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">INVESTIGATE / THE RESEARCH STATION</p><h1>Follow the evidence.<br/><em>Question everything.</em></h1><p class="lead">An observation becomes a question. A question becomes an investigation. The work gets better when we share what we find—and what we still don't know.</p><div class="station-actions"><a class="station-button" href="/investigate/learn/">Explore the research →</a><a class="station-text-link" href="#workbench">Open the workbench ↓</a></div></div>
    <Image src={researchPhoto} alt="Documenting wild mushrooms in the field" widths={[500,850]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 48vw"/>
  </section>
  <section class="station-content" aria-labelledby="station-questions"><div class="station-section-head"><h2 id="station-questions">START WITH A QUESTION</h2><span>THREE WAYS INTO THE EVIDENCE</span></div><div class="station-editorial-grid">
    <a class="station-editorial-card" href="/investigate/learn/"><Image src={fieldPhoto} alt="Landscape explored on a field trip" widths={[300,600]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 30vw"/><span class="station-card-body"><small>01 / SCIENTIFIC PRACTICE</small><strong>What does fungal research actually look like?</strong><span>Explore six research disciplines and how ordinary observations become lasting evidence.</span><b>Explore the guide →</b></span></a>
    <a class="station-editorial-card" href="/investigate/resources/"><Image src={researchPhoto} alt="Field photography and documentation" widths={[300,600]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 30vw"/><span class="station-card-body"><small>02 / REFERENCE MATERIAL</small><strong>Where do we find the original evidence?</strong><span>Sequence databases, herbarium records, literature, and tools to evaluate a claim.</span><b>Browse resources →</b></span></a>
    <a class="station-editorial-card" href="/investigate/tools/"><span class="station-card-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="station-card-body"><small>03 / EXPERIMENTAL TOOLS</small><strong>What can we test ourselves?</strong><span>Workbenches for molecular, ecological, and field questions. Tool maturity and scientific validation are labeled separately.</span><b>Inspect tools →</b></span></a>
  </div></section>
  <section class="station-content station-data" id="field-data"><div class="station-section-head"><h2>FROM THE FIELD</h2><span>REAL OBSERVATIONS / LIVE DATA</span></div><div class="station-data-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">PROJECT SNAPSHOT</p><h2>Crane Hollow Fungal Diversity Survey</h2><p>What can repeated observations tell us about the fungi of a particular place? Explore the live project summary, then follow the original observations to evaluate the evidence yourself.</p><a class="station-text-link" href="/investigate/learn/#surveys">How field surveys work →</a></div><SurveyDashboard client:visible /></div></section>
  <section class="station-content" id="workbench"><div class="station-section-head"><h2>THE RESEARCH WORKBENCH</h2><span>TOOLS / METHODS / LIMITATIONS</span></div><p class="station-tool-intro">Explore the tools we are building to investigate fungal ecology, molecular evidence, and field observations. Availability, software maturity, and independent scientific validation are different questions, and each tool should make those distinctions clear.</p><div class="station-tool-grid">{activeTools.map(tool=><ToolCard tool={tool}/>)}</div><p class="station-footnote">These tools are experimental or planned; none should be treated as a validated species-identification service.</p></section>
</div>
</Base>